{
  "world": 13,
  "name": "the Homesteads",
  "note": "The players' homes (handlers/homes.go, entity/homes.go; claude-notes/player-homes-20261111.md): one zone of the disc where it stands, Tunaria's cell (9, 5), the rim of a crater high over a valley with a lake and a village, and on the rim's southern tip a cottage in its fenced yard, every character's home: the world is built once and every character stands in its own copy of it (an instance, by its owner's character id). The cottage, its low fence, gate, path and stones are Tunaria zone 100's own cottage (a chapel there) carried whole to the rim as the zone's extras, turned to face the valley; outside every side of the fence stand invisible collision boxes (CHAR.ESF's blocker 0x6F412342, collision with nothing to draw, 30 a side) so nobody walks or jumps out. Extras made by the lane's homedecor.py on the rim's own floor. The home block is read by the server, never written into the file: the door a player lands at (on the path before the cottage's door, facing it), the yard's board (the Real Estate Listings' twin, the way out), and the fence's box (a note for tools: nothing is enforced by the server, the blockers are the edge). Built by cmd/worldbuild from the operator's disc.",
